{
  "id": "story-sky",
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "requires": [
    "story",
    "story-sea"
  ],
  "meta": {
    "title": "Act 3 — Sky: The Cirran Shelf",
    "note": "The five main quests of Act 3 (game-story.md §4, issue #145). Act 3 is PART OF THE OPEN WORLD, the way Act 2 is (issue #144): the Shelf is the open world's sky, its towns are CARRIERS that roam above it, and there is no `cirrus` zone. What `sky-revealed` opens is the BALLOON — the means of getting up — not the geography.",
    "loading": "Boot-loaded (see bootstrapContent in main.ts), for the same reason story-sea is: a carried town must exist when the world is built, because the island that carries it is built with the world. The flag-gated load recorded in issue #261 was the zone-era answer and went with the zone.",
    "the-seam": "The ascent is offered at the WRECK on Gullspire by Corwin Vane's sea placement (story-sea.json — the same man, the balloon he patched) and closed by his Skyhaven placement (core.json). Boarding is a `ride` fact the balloon emits, `reach-skyhaven` the arrival replay every town-arrival objective gets. The balloon runs both ways from the first day it is moored: Act 4 stages out of the Encampment.",
    "the-stub": "Quests 3-5 ship as DATA over placeholders (issues #262-#264, #267): `gallery`/`orrery` are Skyhaven's stamping, the Cinderguard and Choirguard wear borrowed rigs, Vess wears Mera's body, and Tobin relights the galleries in one breath. Each placeholder names its issue beside it. No cargo weight (decided). `music:cirrus` ships (issue #267)."
  },
